  "description": "VIYHAO crystallizes in the hexagonal crystal system with space group P 63/m. Reported CIF formula moiety: C24 H36 Cr2 O39 Tb3 3-,25(H2 O1),3(Na1 1+). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Cr1 (Cr) has 6 O neighbors; Tb1A (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb1B (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Cr1I (Cr) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.451-4.015 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 103.37-110.85°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula {[Na(H2O)][Na2Cr2Tb3(μ3-OH)6(L)6(H2O)17]}·16H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 17 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
